WEBVTT

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.370
Get 'im, Rikiishi-san!

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:07.820
Knock him out in one shot!

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.120
Get on with it!

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.980
Rikiishi...

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.340
Our confrontation is finally drawing near.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.610
This time...

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.530
This time we can fight with no hard feelings

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.210
and with our lives on the line!

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.780
You're training hard, Nishi-kun.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.630
Well, keep it up!

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.280
Old man, I feel really great!

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.230
It feels like I'm moving just on impulse! Naturally, you know?

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:17.270
By the way, when's the fight, old man?

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.320
Forget about that.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.970
Shiraki Gym still hasn't sent us a formal challenge.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.350
Come on, don't say it like that.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.250
If I didn't know better, I'd say you didn't want me to fight.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.150
What the hell!?

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.770
Why are you so against me fighting Rikiishi?

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:04.060
He and I still haven't settled our score from juvie.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:07.280
You could say that this was the perfect stage for our showdown!

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.480
You should know that too, old man.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.530
I know. Very well.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.250
But you see...

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.750
But what?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:23.870
But boxing ain't a sport that can abide two winners.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.520
What are you talking about?

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.110
Anyone could tell you that!

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:35.060
And it's gonna be me that wins! Me!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.440
Yeah, it's possible that you'll win.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:48.050
But it's also possible that Rikiishi-kun will win.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:54.080
Wh-What are you trying to say?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.400
Whoever wins in that ring,

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:00.880
in a battle between two such implacable souls,

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.130
is going to spill more than a drop or two of blood.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.870
Rikiishi-kun can become the featherweight champion,

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:24.380
and Joe can become the bantamweight champion.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:31.070
You can fight your respective opponents in your respective rings, and be victorious.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.170
Isn't that enough?

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:40.370
Won't that settle your score from juvie, when you first decided to be a pro boxer?

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.780
Why do you need to go across weight classes

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.920
just to beat the hell out of each other?

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:51.250
This whole thing is utterly immature of both of you!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.050
Don't be stupid, old man.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.220
If that kind of thing is immature,

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.460
then I never want to lose that immaturity!

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.490
Never!

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:33.470
Joe's right.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.700
There are no children and adults when it comes to boxing.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.230
There are only men.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.630
I'm sure Rikiishi feels the same way.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:43.230
Nishi!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.670
Stop slacking off!

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.240
Get back to your drills!

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.490
Y-Yes, sir!

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.800
Geez, I'm surrounded by...

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.020
Hello, everybody!

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.020
<i>Good morning!</i>

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:00.330
Hey, what's up, everyone?

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:05.780
Uh, we came here as soon as possible to congratulate Bro Joe,

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:09.420
for finally getting a chance to settle the score with his fatal foe, Rikiishi...

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.290
Ready, and...

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.120
Congratulations!

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.310
So we all decided to help you out in your practice!

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.310
Help?

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.310
Would that be all right?

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.260
Well, I don't get what's going on,

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.820
but okay.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:28.490
We've got the green light, gentlemen!

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:32.240
I've got the jump rope!

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:34.240
I'll take the sandbag!

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.740
I'll take this thingy!

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.760
Hey, little girl, jump right in!

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.260
What the hell is going on, Nishi?

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.260
I think they made up an excuse to come inside and play since it's so cold and windy outside.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.810
I see! That's some good thinking!

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.280
What are you doing, Joe?

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:02.180
You need to practice!

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:07.730
Hey, little girl... come on! Jump right in!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.530
A cross, huh? Not bad!

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:24.290
Then I'll do Bro Joe's special Double Cross!

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.980
How'd you like that, Tonkichi?

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:30.010
Dammit, not a Triple Cross! Ow!

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.130
Cut it out!

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:54.580
Joe, you'll be sorry if you underestimate Rikiishi.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.520
You should know better than anyone

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:59.410
that he's a cut above Wolf.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.250
So what?

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:02.460
Ah! Ow.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.450
I'm not the man I used to be, either!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.460
I'm nothing like how I was back in juvie.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.580
I still think you're overexerting yourself,

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.470
but what's your weight now?

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.450
121 pounds.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:06.480
I see. You're still three pounds over.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.980
That's if you want to get into Yabuki-kun's bantamweight class.

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:13.050
That would be the case.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.610
Rikiishi-kun, let me be frank.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:23.500
Your frame isn't even cut out for the featherweight class!

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.070
Since you're so strong-willed and diligent,

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:29.730
I kept your food and water intake to the bare minimum

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:33.450
to keep you barely within the featherweight class.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:35.090
But if you lose any more weight...

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.670
it'll be nothing but suicide!

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:51.060
I...

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.320
I can't watch anymore!

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:56.800
I can't watch you get thinner day by day...

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.310
Your eyes sinking into your face...

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:01.810
Rikiishi-kun, I keep asking you.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:06.050
Why do you have to risk your life to fight Yabuki-kun?

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:15.100
He's still a hatchling as a boxer.

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:19.300
He's just a novice who's barely graduated from four-round matches!

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:23.620
But in contrast, you're a boxer who's made a name for himself in the featherweight class.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:26.460
You're even ranked, and you could challenge for the title soon!

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.820
So why would you irrationally lose weight

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:32.310
just to cross gloves with Yabuki-kun?

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:37.450
For what?

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.860
Dinner is served, Miss.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:48.450
Thank you. I'll be right there.

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:55.960
Wait, Rikiishi-kun.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:58.290
I want an answer.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:02.340
My grandfather is becoming quite concerned for you as well.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.850
I have to hear your excuse and explain to him!

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:08.260
Don't press me so hard.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.540
Even I think this is fairly ridiculous,

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.380
so there's no good explanation for this.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:18.770
But if anything, back in juvie...

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.920
I made a promise to him.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.280
That I'd be waiting for him in the professional ring.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:27.780
But he's a bantamweight and you're a featherweight!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.790
And even though we're from different weight classes,

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.750
I can't stand the fact that there's a man who could fight me to a draw.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.270
Not as a man.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.760
B-But...

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:47.120
You probably won't understand no matter how I explain it.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.760
If anything, this is just the nature of a man's world.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.770
A man's world?

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:05.720
Just don't worry about me so much.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.740
Now, your grandfather's waiting in the dining room.

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:12.860
A man's world...

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.700
Sorry we're late.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.530
You seem to have gotten even thinner, Rikiishi-kun.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:20.640
Take mine away.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:26.320
I told you not to give me anything but fruit!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.780
But...

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.280
Rikiishi-kun, I had that prepared for you.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.280
It has just enough calories to keep your body up.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.520
I know.

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:36.500
I'm grateful for your consideration,

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.330
but I have my own calculations.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:41.870
I said take mine away!

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:44.830
My sincere apologies.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.090
I'll just have one of these.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.530
Wait, Rikiishi-kun.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.180
You'd be able to enjoy a fine meal with us

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.990
if you'd just be content with staying in the featherweight class.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:59.760
You could enjoy our chef's cooking to your heart's content!

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:08.830
Enjoy a meal?

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:10.650
Thank you.

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:15.710
But I must reject the offer of Shiraki Gym, which has the nation's finest facilities,

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:19.930
and fight a man who climbed to the top, covered in blood, from a tiny gym under a bridge.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.410
He waited for me in a place

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:26.970
with no dazzling lights or warm mattresses.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.780
That's who Yabuki is!

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:08.700
Where've you been, Joe!?

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.580
Idiot! What if you catch a cold?

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:11.320
Come inside at once!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:14.120
I know. I have my match with Rikiishi coming up.

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.290
I won't push myself.

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:53.020
Where are you going, Rikiishi-kun?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:56.030
I'm going to start sleeping in the gym from now on.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:01.740
Tonight, I say goodbye to the luxury of the Shiraki mansion.

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:05.750
I don't plan on coming back until after my match with Yabuki.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.710
Good night, Miss.

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:15.510
Rikiishi-kun!

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.780
Rikiishi-kun!

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:12.700
Rikiishi-san! What are you doing here so late?

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:26.190
Are you all right, Rikiishi-san?

00:21:26.190 --> 00:21:27.650
Rikiishi-san!

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:31.060
I'm going to start sleeping in the basement storeroom from now on.

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:34.460
And while I'm here, I have something to ask of you.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:37.770
Once I'm inside, lock the door.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:40.070
B-But that's crazy!

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.710
I'm counting on you.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:57.330
R-Rikiishi-san! Why?

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:59.380
Why?

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:00.870
Why?

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:03.630
Why?

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:04.960
Why?

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:08.130
To win against Yabuki,

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:09.830
and in my battle to lose weight!

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:13.170
When losing weight, the thirst is more unbearable than the hunger.

00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:17.140
This is to ensure that I don't give in to temptation

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:21.150
and lunge at a water faucet during the night!

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:27.320
I must defeat Yabuki!

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:42.170
Everyone!

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:43.150
What's the matter?

00:22:43.150 --> 00:22:44.240
Where's Rikiishi-kun?

00:22:44.240 --> 00:22:45.510
He's in the storeroom!

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:47.050
He locked himself in...

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:32.300
Rikiishi-kun...

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:36.140
You're turning pale in the darkness denying yourself everything.

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:40.550
And you call this a man's world?

00:23:52.230 --> 00:23:57.080
Rikiishi's weight loss is a hellish scene filled with bloodlust and madness.

00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:01.370
And when Joe learns of Rikiishi's condition, he becomes even more tense.

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:05.410
And when he sees his companion Nishi stray from his weight loss plan,

00:24:05.410 --> 00:24:07.040
Joe's anger explodes!

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:10.390
Now, as his match with Rikiishi is scheduled,

00:24:10.390 --> 00:24:12.700
and Joe is more nervous than ever before,

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:14.010
which way is tomorrow!?

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:30.900
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:30.900
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:31.990 --> 00:24:34.740
Oira boxer

00:24:31.990 --> 00:24:34.740
I am a boxer.

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:42.660
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:42.660
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:44.210 --> 00:24:48.170
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:44.210 --> 00:24:48.170
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:48.170 --> 00:24:50.210
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:48.170 --> 00:24:50.210
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:52.300 --> 00:24:56.430
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:52.300 --> 00:24:56.430
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:56.430 --> 00:24:59.430
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:56.430 --> 00:24:59.430
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:04.060
Yuke kouya wo

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:04.060
Go to the wilderness!

00:25:05.270 --> 00:25:07.770
Oira boxer

00:25:05.270 --> 00:25:07.770
I am a boxer.

00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:16.030
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:16.030
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!
